# External paths hooks may access outside the harness root, in addition
# to repos/ and worktree/. This file is a copy-ready template only —
# hooks never read it; run `cp .env.sample .env` (or write your own
# .env) to opt in. No .env means no external access, exactly like an
# empty ALLOWED_EXT_DIRS. Comma or colon separated; supports a leading
# `~` for $HOME. There is no blanket "allow everything" switch.
#
# Hooks read .env from the checkout root AND the lab root (the directory
# holding repos/ + worktree/); both lists are combined. Put a single
# .env at the lab root to cover every checkout on the machine. Changes
# apply on the next tool call — .env is read per hook invocation.
ALLOWED_EXT_DIRS=/tmp,~/.claude,~/.codex,~/.config/devin,~/.gemini
